window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-6a28e2fac99eeca8"]={"key":"ny_c-6a28e2fac99eeca8","group":"ny_c","uid":"6a28e2fac99eeca8","rank":18,"title":"cavendish housing handler briefing pack","occupation":"editors","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are the editor preparing Cavendish Housing Trust's contact-centre briefing pack for Efua Oyelaran, Gerhard Gauthier, Mariam Bhandari, Joaquin Karlsson and Milena Navarro, who will use it with the other eight handlers on their first day back in January. Our operations lead, Iris Baranowski, needs one practical pack covering every material change that may land between January and next April for residents asking about rent, service charges or support funds. The list is not held in one place: notices and determinations from the regulator, council web pages, scheme guidance, and our board minutes do not always use the same commencement date, and some matters are still consultations rather than decisions. Bellwether Instruments supports our contact-centre platform and Drakemoor Laboratories administers one of the support-fund assessment services, so notices from those organisations may also be mentioned in the material we receive, but the pack must stay focused on what a handler can accurately tell a resident. Create Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx in the top level of the working directory, using exactly that filename. Keep it to no more than six pages, make it easy to scan during a live call, and include a change schedule, plain-English notes for each change, and a compact Q&A card. Compare the current period with the January-to-April period and call out material differences, including any change whose timing or status is not settled. Show what has changed in this edition and identify the basis and confidence of each important statement; do not invent a date, rate, threshold, entitlement, or system action where the available information does not support it. The handlers need language they can use with residents, but they are not benefits advisers, lawyers, rent officers or complaint investigators, so make the boundary and escalation points usable without turning the pack into a separate specialist procedure. Please make the finished document something a new handler can use without asking its author what a status label, date, resident impact or escalation instruction means.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx` — A concise handler briefing pack containing a change schedule, plain-English explanations, period comparison, source and confidence indications, edition-change record, boundary guidance, and a compact resident Q&A card. (Must be no more than six pages when rendered.; Must be written for eleven contact-centre handlers using it during live resident calls.; Must distinguish confirmed, proposed or consulted-on, and unresolved timing.; Must not invent unsupported dates, rates, thresholds, entitlements, or system instructions.; Must be practical to scan and must stand alone without an author briefing.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx","bytes":44714,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/e7eee873fa57f8fa6646620943b2857a0366254d9e964b6e7dbd719b104273b6.docx","sha256":"e7eee873fa57f8fa6646620943b2857a0366254d9e964b6e7dbd719b104273b6","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CAVENDISH  |  HOUSING TRUST\nHandler briefing pack\nFor Efua Oyelaran, Gerhard Gauthier, Mariam Bhandari, Joaquin Karlsson, Milena Navarro and eight fellow contact-centre handlers.\nCOVERAGE HORIZON\nJanuary through the following April\nCompare with the current period (information in force before the January return).\nUSE THIS PACK TO\nExplain published position • qualify what is pending • route account or specialist questions.\nDo not promise a rate, date, payment or outcome unless confirmed.\nAt a glance\nRent, service charges and support funds do not share one automatic annual cycle. A decision, its effective date and resident-facing implementation may be different events.\nStatus is explicit: CONFIRMED = usable as fact; PROPOSED / CONSULTED-ON = not in force; UNRESOLVED TIMING = subject or decision may exist, but commencement or implementation is not reliable.\nWhen sources conflict, record the conflict, use the narrower safe wording, and refer for confirmation. A publication date is not automatically an operative date.\nConfidence key\nHIGH\nMEDIUM\nLOW / PENDING\nHIGH: primary determination/approved Trust record is consistent.  MEDIUM: attributed guidance or operational notice, useful but needs scope check.  LOW / PENDING: consultation, conflicting dates or missing confirmation; never state as settled.\nScope guard\nThis is an information aid, not a benefits, legal, rent-officer or complaint-investigation procedure. Explain the published position; do not decide eligibility, interpret rights, amend an account, or investigate a complaint. Escalation directions are on page 4.\n\n\n1 | Change schedule — January to April\nRead each row across: subject → status → timing → resident impact → handler treatment. “Basis” identifies the source type available to the editor; no unsupported rate or threshold is inserted.\nID / subject\nStatus + confidence\nTiming (what is known)\nResident impact\nHandler treatment / basis\nR1  Rent review / annual formula\nCONFIRMED  • HIGH\nTrust decision is recorded for the January–April period; exact effective date and amount are not reproduced here. Announcement, effective date and billing implementation must be checked separately.\nA rent amount may differ from the current period when the Trust’s notice takes effect; no figure is promised in this pack.\nSay: “A rent review is confirmed, but I must check the notice for your tenancy’s effective date and amount.” Basis: approved Trust/board record; confirm account application with Rent Accounts.\nR2  Rent policy consultation\nPROPOSED / CONSULTED-ON  • LOW / PENDING\nConsultation or regulator material discusses a possible rule change during the horizon; no implementation decision or date is confirmed.\nA possible future rule is not a current entitlement or charge.\nSay “This is being considered, not implemented.” Do not forecast a rate. Basis: regulator notice / consultation; route policy questions to Housing Policy.\nS1  Service-charge estimate\nCONFIRMED  • HIGH\nAnnual estimate is issued on its service schedule; it may be dated differently from rent. Actual-cost reconciliation, if any, follows the service-charge process.\nThe service-charge line can move while rent does not, or vice versa. It represents services, not rent.\nSay: “Your service charge pays for listed services and follows its own estimate/reconciliation.” Basis: approved service-charge budget/Trust notice; account-specific queries to Service Charge Team.\nS2  Service cost / energy pass-through\nUNRESOLVED TIMING  • MEDIUM\nProvider cost information and Trust review are available, but commencement/implementation date is not settled; do not select the earliest date seen.\nAny later adjustment may be shown on a service-charge statement, subject to confirmation and notice.\nSay “We are checking the effective date; no change is confirmed from this notice alone.” Basis: provider notice + Trust review; escalate timing conflict to Service Charge Team.\nF1  Support-fund assessment service\nPROPOSED / CONSULTED-ON  • LOW / PENDING\nDrakemoor Laboratories notice describes a possible assessment-service/process change; Trust adoption and start date are not confirmed.\nA process change would not itself guarantee an award or change eligibility.\nSay “Assessment is still subject to the published scheme and decision.” Basis: Drakemoor notice (administrator evidence, not Trust authority); route assessment questions to Welfare/Support Fund Team.\nF2  Support-fund allocation / availability\nUNRESOLVED TIMING  • LOW / PENDING\nCouncil or scheme guidance indicates a funding window may change between January and April; allocation, threshold and start date await confirmation.\nA fund being open or replenished does not mean every resident receives payment.\nSay “We can record your question and refer it for an eligibility decision; I cannot promise funding.” Basis: council web guidance / scheme guidance; Welfare/Support Fund Team.\nF3  External platform notice\nCONFIRMED AS NOTICE ONLY  • MEDIUM\nBellwether Instruments may change contact-centre platform wording or display; no Trust resident charge or entitlement follows automatically.\nA screen or message may look different; it does not change the resident’s rent or support outcome by itself.\nTreat as supporting evidence only. Follow current approved Trust wording and report a mismatch to the contact-centre lead; do not invent a click path. Basis: Bellwether notice.\nStatus labels are operational: “confirmed” means the underlying decision is usable as fact, not that every account has already been updated. “Notice only” is not a resident outcome.\n\n\n2 | Plain-English notes & period comparison\nWhat to say about each topic\nRent — Rent is the charge for the home. The confirmed review may change the amount from the effective date in the Trust notice. It is separate from service charges and does not establish support-fund eligibility. If the resident’s account differs from the general notice, stop and refer to Rent Accounts.\nService charges — A service charge pays for specified services and is estimated or reconciled on its own timetable. A service-charge movement is not automatically a rent change. Explain the statement line and the relevant notice; do not calculate or infer a future amount when timing is unresolved.\nSupport funds — A support fund is a scheme or allocation that may help eligible residents. An open window, administrator notice or assessment-process change is not a guaranteed award. Eligibility, evidence and award decisions belong to the assessment/welfare function.\nTiming rule — The familiar “one annual housing change” assumption stops applying when rent, service-charge and fund decisions have different decision, effective or implementation dates. In this horizon, R1 and S1 demonstrate separate cycles; S2 and F2 remain conditional.\nCurrent period → January–April comparison\nTopic\nCurrent period (before January return)\nJanuary–April position\nWhy it matters on a call\nRent\nExisting published rent information remains the reference until a valid Trust notice applies.\nR1 review is confirmed; amount/effective date must come from the resident notice. R2 remains only a proposal.\nDo not merge a proposed policy with the operative rent or quote a figure without the notice.\nService charges\nCurrent estimate/statement is the reference for the current period.\nS1 follows its service schedule; S2 may be reviewed but has no settled start date.\nA resident can see rent and service charge move at different times and for different reasons.\nSupport funds\nExisting scheme/assessment route applies unless the administering body says otherwise.\nF1 process proposal and F2 funding timing are pending; no automatic award follows.\nRecord the question and refer rather than promise eligibility, payment or a date.\nWhen information conflicts\nName the source type and the event it describes (announcement, decision, effective date or implementation).\nIf dates differ, do not choose one: use “date not confirmed” and refer to the owning team. The resident-facing answer is limited to what is consistent across sources.\nIf no reliable confirmation supports an answer, say so plainly, capture the minimum facts and escalate. This is a safe limitation, not a promise of a later outcome.\n\n\n3 | Live-call Q&A card\nResident asks…\nHandler answer (use or adapt)\nWhat is changing?\nThere is a confirmed rent review and a confirmed service-charge estimate on separate schedules. Some policy, cost and support-fund items are proposed or still being timed. I can check the notice that applies to your account; this pack does not contain a rate or guarantee.\nWhen does it change?\nThe announcement, effective date and the date it appears on an account may differ. Rent and service charges can have different dates; for S2 and F2 the start date is not confirmed. I will not guess—your owning team can confirm the applicable notice.\nDoes it apply to me?\nIt depends on your tenancy, service schedule and (for a fund) the scheme assessment. I can explain the general published position, but I cannot decide an individual account, eligibility or award.\nWhy did my rent and service charge not move together?\nThey are separate charges with separate bases and timetables. Rent follows the rent notice; service charge follows the services estimate or reconciliation. A difference does not by itself indicate an error.\nIs the support fund guaranteed?\nNo. An open fund or assessment-process notice is not a guaranteed payment. Eligibility, evidence and the award decision sit with the Welfare/Support Fund Team or scheme administrator.\nI saw a different date / message.\nThank you—sources can describe different events. I will record the wording and date, avoid treating it as final, and refer the conflict to the owning team for confirmation.\nBoundaries & escalation\nDo not decide / provide\nSay instead\nRoute + capture before referral\nBenefits eligibility or specialist assessment\n“I can explain the published scheme position, not decide eligibility or an award.”\nWelfare / Support Fund Team or named scheme assessor. Capture fund/topic, relevant date, resident question, and any stated deadline.\nLegal advice or interpretation of rights\n“I cannot give legal advice or interpret your rights.”\nLegal Counsel / approved rights service. Capture the issue, document/date cited, and resident’s question—do not offer a view.\nAccount-specific rent/service-charge determination\n“The general note cannot decide what is on your account.”\nRent Accounts or Service Charge Team. Capture account reference, charge line, notice/date, and mismatch described.\nComplaint investigation or outcome\n“I can record the concern, but I cannot investigate or decide it here.”\nComplaints function. Capture concern, event/date, requested outcome and relevant correspondence.\n\n\n4 | Edition record, sources & handoff\nWhat changed in this edition\nAffected topic\nEdition change\nHandler consequence\nAll topics / timing\nAdded explicit decision → effective date → implementation convention and conflict treatment.\nDo not equate publication with a live account change.\nRent + service charges\nSeparated rent review (R1) from service-charge estimate/reconciliation (S1) and unresolved cost timing (S2).\nExplain why charges may move apart; refer mismatches.\nSupport funds\nAdded proposed assessment-service item (F1) and unresolved allocation timing (F2), with no automatic-award wording.\nQualify every fund answer; route eligibility.\nCall handling\nAdded Q&A card, status/confidence key and boundary routes.\nUse the scripts; capture facts before referral.\nSource register (source type, scope and confidence)\nSource type used\nWhat it can support\nLimits / treatment\nApproved Trust / board record\nConfirmed rent or service-charge decision and internal scope.\nStill check notice, effective date and account implementation separately.\nRegulator notice or consultation\nA policy position, proposal or consultation status.\nNot a Trust implementation or resident entitlement until adopted and effective.\nCouncil or scheme guidance\nExternal funding window or scheme process information.\nAttribution required; thresholds, allocations and dates remain pending if not confirmed.\nProvider notice — Bellwether Instruments / Drakemoor Laboratories\nEvidence about platform display or an assessment service.\nSupporting evidence only; does not create a Trust-wide charge, award or system instruction.\nQuick handoff checklist\nCapture resident question, subject (rent / service charge / fund), relevant notice or date, account or tenancy context, and the uncertainty or mismatch reported.\nUse “confirmed”, “proposed / consulted-on” or “unresolved timing” exactly as defined. Never fill a gap with an estimated rate, threshold, payment, date or outcome.\nThis pack is current for the January–April planning horizon; the owning team’s later approved notice supersedes it. No other topic is changed by this edition unless listed above.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submission is a readable DOCX file named Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted filename and successful DOCX parsing.","grader_hint":"Check the top-level filename and that the file opens as a valid Word document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered briefing pack is no more than six pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with an offline office renderer and count pages; six or fewer earns credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Cavendish Housing Trust and its intended audience as contact-centre handlers.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Title, subtitle, or audience statement.","grader_hint":"Look for both the Trust identity and a clear handler audience statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states the January-to-next-April operating horizon.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Coverage-period statement.","grader_hint":"Accept an equivalent statement that the pack covers January through the following April."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule covers all three requested subject areas: rent, service charges, and support funds.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule entries or clearly labelled subject groups.","grader_hint":"Verify that each subject area has at least one substantive change or status entry, not merely a mention in the title."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule presents multiple distinct changes or change topics rather than one generic annual update.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Distinct schedule rows or cards.","grader_hint":"Count substantively different change topics; repeated wording for one change does not qualify as coverage."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each schedule entry has an identifiable subject, status, timing, resident impact, and handler-facing treatment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule fields and linked notes.","grader_hint":"Walk every change row; award only if all five dimensions can be located without inference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule distinguishes confirmed changes from consultations or proposals.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Status labels or equivalent wording.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit labels such as confirmed, proposed, consulted-on, pending, or equivalent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not present a consultation or proposal as an implemented change.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison of status labels with wording in notes and Q&A.","grader_hint":"Check that future or uncertain matters use conditional language and are not described as current entitlements or charges."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Where commencement dates differ or remain unsettled, the document preserves the uncertainty and gives a safe operational interpretation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing fields and explanatory notes.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit unresolved or conflicting-date treatment rather than a silently selected date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes an announcement, decision, effective date, and resident-facing implementation where those are not the same event.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Date/status language in schedule or notes.","grader_hint":"Award when the artifact avoids treating publication date as automatically equal to operative date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack includes an explicit basis or source-type indication for each material change.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source or basis column, footnotes, or linked note labels.","grader_hint":"Accept regulator determination, council page, scheme guidance, board minute, provider notice, or a clearly marked professional basis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack does not fabricate citations, URLs, document numbers, or quotations to create false authority.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source register and in-text references.","grader_hint":"Check whether references are specific only where supportable and whether uncertain provenance is labelled rather than invented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Important quantitative or eligibility claims are either supported by an identified basis or explicitly withheld pending confirmation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rates, thresholds, dates, and entitlement wording.","grader_hint":"A restrained 'not confirmed' treatment earns credit when a precise value cannot be justified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document includes a confidence or certainty indication for important statements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Confidence labels, certainty key, or equivalent.","grader_hint":"Verify that the labels are defined and used on substantive entries."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The confidence convention distinguishes confirmed information from information awaiting confirmation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legend and examples.","grader_hint":"A legend alone is insufficient; inspect whether entries use it consistently."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack compares the current period with the January-to-April period.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison table or explicit before/after section.","grader_hint":"Require two identifiable periods and substantive comparison, not merely two date headings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The period comparison explains why each material difference matters to a resident or handler.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Impact or meaning column in the comparison.","grader_hint":"A numerical or date difference without operational meaning does not earn this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states when the familiar assumption that a housing change follows one annual cycle stops applying across the covered topics.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing guidance and examples.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit exception principle covering differing cycles, mid-year changes, consultations, or service-specific timing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The timing exception is applied to at least two different subject areas rather than stated abstractly.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rent, service-charge, or support-fund examples.","grader_hint":"Verify that the artifact demonstrates the exception with concrete schedule entries."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack explains rent changes in plain language suitable for a resident.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rent note or Q&A response.","grader_hint":"Look for an intelligible explanation of what changes, when, and what remains unknown."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Rent wording separates the rent amount or rule from any separate service charge or support-fund issue.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rent explanation and cross-references.","grader_hint":"Award when the document avoids presenting all resident payments as one undifferentiated change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack explains service-charge changes in plain language suitable for a resident.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Service-charge note or Q&A response.","grader_hint":"The explanation must address what a service charge represents and how timing or amount may differ from rent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Service-charge wording avoids implying that every service-charge movement is a rent change.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions and resident-facing wording.","grader_hint":"Check for a clear distinction between the two categories."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack explains support-fund changes in plain language suitable for a resident.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Support-fund note or Q&A response.","grader_hint":"The explanation must cover status, timing, and the fact that a fund-related change may not equal automatic payment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Support-fund wording distinguishes availability or process changes from a guaranteed individual award.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Eligibility and outcome language.","grader_hint":"Look for careful treatment of assessment, eligibility, funding limits, or pending decisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document defines or explains every status label used in the schedule.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Legend or inline definitions.","grader_hint":"Test all labels, including abbreviations and confidence markers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A handler can tell from each entry whether the change is already in force, future-dated, conditional, or not yet confirmed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Combined status and timing fields.","grader_hint":"Walk representative entries from each status category."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack includes a compact Q&A card.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Clearly labelled Q&A card or equivalent quick-reference block.","grader_hint":"Require a distinct, quickly scannable component rather than scattered questions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Q&A card covers a resident asking what is changing, when it changes, and whether it applies to them.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Questions and answers in the card.","grader_hint":"All three resident concerns must be directly represented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Q&A card includes a response for an unsettled or consulted-on change.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conditional Q&A entry.","grader_hint":"The response must avoid presenting a pending matter as final."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Q&A card includes a response for a resident who asks why their rent and service charge do not move together.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Relevant Q&A wording.","grader_hint":"Look for a concise explanation of separate bases or timing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Q&A card includes a response for a resident asking whether a support fund is guaranteed.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Relevant Q&A wording.","grader_hint":"The response must preserve assessment or eligibility uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack tells handlers what they may state as fact and what they must qualify as pending, estimated, or unconfirmed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Handler language guidance.","grader_hint":"Look for usable phrasing or a factual-versus-conditional convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack gives a clear boundary that handlers must not determine specialist benefits eligibility.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary or escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"The document must prohibit overstepping, not merely name another team."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack gives a clear boundary that handlers must not provide legal advice or interpret a resident's legal rights.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary wording.","grader_hint":"Accept a direct limitation paired with an appropriate referral."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack gives a clear boundary that handlers must not make or investigate a rent-account or complaint determination outside their role.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Role-limit statement.","grader_hint":"Look for a distinction between explaining published information and deciding a case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each specialist boundary is paired with a practical escalation or referral direction.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation matrix or adjacent instructions.","grader_hint":"A prohibition without a usable destination earns no credit for this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies a route for questions about individual rent or service-charge account application.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"Accept a named internal function or role, without requiring an invented local code."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies a route for support-fund eligibility or assessment questions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"Accept the relevant assessment or welfare-support function."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies a route for legal or rights-based questions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"Accept legal counsel or an appropriate specialist service."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Escalation guidance tells the handler what information to capture before referral.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Referral checklist or call-handling note.","grader_hint":"Require useful minimum context such as resident question, affected charge or fund, relevant date, and uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack avoids instructing handlers to promise a payment, fixed amount, implementation date, or outcome that is not confirmed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Q&A and handler-language review.","grader_hint":"Check examples and scripts for promises; conditional wording is required where status is uncertain."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack tells handlers how to respond when the resident's circumstances or account do not match the general change note.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception or escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"Look for a stop-and-check or referral principle rather than a blanket application rule."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document records what changed in this edition.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change log, edition note, or revision statement.","grader_hint":"Require substantive change description, not only a version number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The edition-change record identifies the affected topic and the nature of the change.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change-log entries.","grader_hint":"Each listed revision should be traceable to rent, service charges, support funds, timing, status, or guidance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies items that remain unchanged or are outside the current confirmed scope where that distinction prevents handler confusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or 'no change' note.","grader_hint":"Award when the pack prevents an implied change from being inferred merely because a topic is discussed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document treats notices from external or supporting organisations as evidence to assess, not automatic authority over Cavendish resident outcomes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source/boundary treatment involving external notices.","grader_hint":"Check that external information is contextualised and not converted into an unsupported Trust commitment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack distinguishes Trust-level information from information belonging to a council, regulator, scheme administrator, or specialist provider.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source labels and boundary notes.","grader_hint":"Look for attribution and scope, especially for support-fund material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document provides a consistent treatment for conflicting information rather than selecting the most convenient date or statement without explanation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conflict note, status convention, or schedule examples.","grader_hint":"Award when the artifact records the conflict, limits the claim, and identifies what must be confirmed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The schedule and plain-English notes agree on status and timing for every covered change.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-reading schedule against notes.","grader_hint":"Sample all entries; contradictions in date or certainty fail this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Q&A answers agree with the schedule and notes on the same change topics.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-reading Q&A against the rest of the pack.","grader_hint":"Check that quick-reference wording does not simplify away a material qualification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack uses resident-friendly language and explains unavoidable technical terms.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered text and definitions.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a new handler could repeat the wording to a resident without translating unexplained jargon."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pack is genuinely usable during a live call: headings, status cues, tables, and Q&A content allow a handler to find the relevant answer quickly.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should test several likely resident questions and judge navigation, scanability, and legibility rather than rewarding decoration."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pack is self-contained enough for a new handler to use without asking its author what a status, date, resident impact, or escalation instruction means.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole rendered artifact.","grader_hint":"Judge practical independence; unexplained labels, vague referrals, or missing links between schedule and Q&A should lose credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pack states what handlers should do when no reliable confirmation supports an answer, without turning that statement into an invented system procedure.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Uncertainty and escalation guidance.","grader_hint":"Look for a safe limitation-and-referral approach, while confirming that no fabricated software click path or internal code is required."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is an enterprise housing contact-centre briefing artifact for handlers answering resident questions about rent, service charges, and support funds across a changing January-to-April operating period. The editor must turn dispersed and partly conflicting policy information into a restrained, usable, evidence-aware document without crossing into specialist advice.","difficulty_sources":["The schedule of changes must be assembled from professional knowledge rather than supplied source files.","The document must distinguish confirmed changes from consultations and unresolved commencement dates.","A commonly used annual-change assumption does not apply uniformly across rent, service charges, and support funds.","Support-fund and benefits content overlaps with specialist functions, requiring a clear boundary without giving legal or eligibility advice."],"authoring_plan":{"artifact":{"filename":"Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx","purpose":"Create a compact, reusable handler-facing normative pack with a schedule, explanatory notes, comparison, edition record, boundaries, and Q&A card.","content_constraints":["Use a January-to-next-April horizon and compare it with the current period.","Include the three subject domains: rent, service charges, and support funds.","Use generic but professionally plausible recurring change categories; do not rely on live facts or invented exact figures.","Mark confirmed, proposed or consulted-on, and unresolved items distinctly.","Make uncertain or unsupported values visibly conditional or pending.","Include source-type attribution without fabricating citations.","Include a plain-language resident impact and a handler-facing statement for each material item.","Include a timing convention explaining that the familiar annual cycle is not universal: rent, service charges, and support funds can follow different decision, effective, and implementation dates.","Include boundaries for benefits eligibility, legal advice or rights interpretation, account-specific determinations, and complaint investigation, with a useful specialist destination for each.","Include an edition-change record and a defined status/confidence legend.","Keep the rendered artifact at six pages or fewer."]},"gold_derivation":{"coverage_model":["At least six substantively distinct change topics spanning the three subject domains, including at least one confirmed-style item, one consulted-on or proposed item, and one unresolved-timing item.","For each topic, derive a tuple of subject, status, timing, basis, confidence, resident impact, handler wording, and escalation condition.","Derive the period comparison from the same topic tuples so the comparison cannot contradict the schedule.","Derive Q&A prompts from likely live-call questions: what changed, when, whether it applies, why rent and service charges differ, whether support is guaranteed, and what to do when information is pending.","Derive boundary checks from the occupational distinction between explaining published information and making specialist eligibility, legal, account, or complaint decisions.","Derive the rule-of-thumb check from the annual-cycle assumption and require the artifact to identify exceptions across at least two subject areas.","Derive the external-organisation check by requiring attribution and scope treatment for notices associated with Bellwether Instruments or Drakemoor Laboratories, without making either organisation the source of a Trust-wide entitlement."],"review_method":"Render the DOCX offline, inspect page count and legibility, then walk the schedule row by row and cross-check every corresponding note and Q&A answer. Test the artifact with hypothetical questions about a confirmed rent change, a pending service-charge matter, an unresolved support-fund date, a mismatched resident circumstance, and a legal or eligibility question."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"briefing_pack","filename":"Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise handler briefing pack containing a change schedule, plain-English explanations, period comparison, source and confidence indications, edition-change record, boundary guidance, and a compact resident Q&A card.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be no more than six pages when rendered.","Must be written for eleven contact-centre handlers using it during live resident calls.","Must distinguish confirmed, proposed or consulted-on, and unresolved timing.","Must not invent unsupported dates, rates, thresholds, entitlements, or system instructions.","Must be practical to scan and must stand alone without an author briefing."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"professional_report","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"editors","sector":"information","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent document reviewer inspect the rendered DOCX against every rubric item, with a second reviewer adjudicating status/timing consistency, scope boundaries, unsupported claims, and live-call usability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["Because no source files are supplied and live internet is forbidden, the gold standard evaluates professional structure, restraint, attribution, uncertainty handling, and occupationally reasonable coverage rather than exact current regulatory rates or dates.","Reviewers should not require invented local escalation codes, URLs, staff names, or exact policy thresholds."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:46:39+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:46:39+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:46:39+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:46:39+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R17', 'R55']","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:46:39+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/6a28e2fac99eeca8","declared_deliverables":["Cavendish_handler_briefing_pack.docx"]};
